 SUNCT, according to the <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b4-co-2-533">International Headache Society Classification Committee (2004)</xref></p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cluster headache</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CPH</th><th colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">SUNCT<hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0201c;Regular criteria&#x0201d;<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn7-co-2-533">1</xref></th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0201c;New proposal&#x0201d;<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn7-co-2-533">1</xref> (or &#x0201c;SUNA&#x0201d;)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1"><bold>Autonomic phenomena</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1. Conjunctival injection and/or tearing</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+ only &#x0201c;and&#x0201d;; &#x0201c;or&#x0201d; omitted</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2. Nasal congestion and/or rhinorrhea</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3. Eyelid edema</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4. Forehead and facial sweating</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5. Miosis and/or ptosis</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1"><bold>Diagnostic requirement</bold></td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">At least one of the features: 1&#x02013;5); for SUNA, one of the features: 1&#x02013;3</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn7-co-2-533"><label>1</label><p><bold>Notes:</bold> <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b5-co-2-533">The International Classification of Headache Disorders 2004.</xref></p></fn><fn id="tfn8-co-2-533"><p><bold>Abbreviation:</bold> CPH, chronic paroxysmal hemicrania.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>